{"term":"tongue","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:14238f9f2f17979faf","definition":"The flexible muscular organ in the mouth that is used to move food around, for tasting and that is moved into various positions to modify the flow of air from the lungs in order to produce different sounds in speech.","example":"But lering and lurking here and there like ſpies,","pos":"noun","synonyms":["glossa","lingua"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["👅"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tongue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4239f79ec57ee350d7","definition":"Such an organ, as taken from animals and used for food (especially from cows).","example":"cold tongue with mustard","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["👅"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tongue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:416428bd36296a2e8d","definition":"Any similar organ, such as the lingual ribbon, or odontophore, of a mollusk; the proboscis of a moth or butterfly; or the lingua of an insect.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["👅"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tongue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0d9ccae7ba45212b31","definition":"A language.","example":"He was speaking in his native tongue.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["idiom","language","lingo"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"metonymically","register":"countable, metonymically, uncountable","wordFamily":["👅"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attributio